# Code formatting

- Run `dart format .` and `flutter analyze` before every commit, and fix
  everything they report. CI ("Format, analyze, and test") is a required
  check on `main`, so an unformatted or failing pull request cannot merge.
- Never commit with `--no-verify`. The pre-commit hook
  (`tool/git-hooks/pre-commit`) formats staged Dart files for you; if it
  fails, fix the cause.
- Never hand-edit generated files (`*.g.dart`, `*.mocks.dart`,
  `lib/l10n/generated/`); regenerate them (`dart run build_runner build`,
  `flutter gen-l10n`).

See CLAUDE.md, "Code formatting", for the shared rule.
